body:
`normalizeMessage()` assumes each `raw.parts[]` element is a non-null object and does property access (`p.type`, `p.text`). A malformed request like `parts: [null]` will throw at runtime and return 500. Consider defensively validating/coercing `parts` elements (skip non-objects/nulls) so normalization cannot crash on untrusted input.
```suggestion
    const textParts: string[] = [];

    for (const part of raw.parts as unknown[]) {
      if (typeof part !== 'object' || part === null) {
        continue;
      }

      const partObj = part as Record<string, unknown>;
      if (partObj.type === 'text' && typeof partObj.text === 'string') {
        textParts.push(partObj.text);
      }
    }
```
